<emu-clause id="formal-permanent-steps">
  <h1>Residue Steps Without a Meaning of Their Own</h1>
  <p>Each <code>emu-permanent</code> names a residue step, by clause (<code>sec-x</code>, or <code>sec-x#n</code> for its n-th algorithm) or overlay algorithm and step path, that the base layer leaves unread on purpose. Class <code>assert-provenance</code> is an Assert about where a value or a call came from; <code>assert-future</code> is an Assert about what a later step or the caller will do; neither has a test on the state at its step, and Assert steps are strictly informative (<emu-xref href="#sec-algorithm-conventions"></emu-xref>). <code>informative</code> is a NOTE's alternative algorithm, which the normative steps do not use. <code>history</code> is a test on what an object's internal methods have returned before, which the state does not record.</p>

  <emu-permanent clause="sec-arguments-exotic-objects-defineownproperty-p-desc" step="7.b.i.1" class="assert-future">The success of the following Set, a later step, for the reason that mapped formal parameters are writable.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-arguments-exotic-objects-set-p-v-receiver" step="3.a" class="assert-future">The success of the following Set, a later step, for the reason that mapped formal parameters are writable.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-createimportbinding" step="2" class="assert-future">What _targetModule_.[[Environment]] will have once it is instantiated, a later state.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-date" step="4.c.ii.1" class="assert-future">The next step's completion, for the reason that _primitive_ is a String.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-evaldeclarationinstantiation" step="3.c" class="assert-future">Termination of the following loop.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-evaldeclarationinstantiation" step="13.b.ii.3" class="assert-future">Termination of the following loop.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-getexportednames" step="3.a" class="assert-provenance">Why _module_ is in _exportStarSet_ (the start of an export-star cycle), not a further test.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-makebasicobject" step="6" class="assert-future">Conditioned on which internal methods the caller will later override.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-makebasicobject" step="7" class="assert-future">Conditioned on which internal methods the caller will later override.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-moduleevaluation" step="1" class="assert-provenance">About the surrounding agent's other calls to Evaluate, which the state at the step does not record.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-ordinarysetwithowndescriptor" step="2.d.i" class="assert-provenance">Rests on _receiver_'s [[GetOwnProperty]] answer just before; a Proxy receiver need not keep it, so the Assert is vacuous there (a drafted spec issue).</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-preparefortailcall" step="1" class="assert-future">What later evaluation will and will not use the current execution context for.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-resolveexport" step="3.a.i" class="assert-provenance">Why the request is in _resolveSet_ (a circular import), not a further test.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-resolveexport" step="9.e.iii.1" class="assert-provenance">Why this branch is reached (a second star export resolves the name), not a further test.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-runtime-semantics-classdefinitionevaluation" step="6.a.i.1" class="assert-provenance">Why a duplicate private name can occur (a getter/setter pair), which the early errors guarantee.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-runtime-semantics-evaluateclassstaticblockbody" step="1" class="assert-provenance">Which step created _funcObj_ is its origin, not a property of the function object.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="erratum-AtomicsWaitAsyncTimeoutAssert/sec-enqueueatomicswaitasynctimeoutjob@1.b.ii/proposed" step="1" class="assert-provenance">Compares the host's clock readings while ignoring their non-monotonicity, which the state does not give.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="definition-sec-getprototypefromconstructor-1/sec-getprototypefromconstructor@1/definition" step="2" class="assert-provenance">What the caller intends the intrinsic object for, not a property of the object or the state.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="definition-sec-ordinarycreatefromconstructor-1/sec-ordinarycreatefromconstructor@1/definition" step="2" class="assert-provenance">What the caller intends the intrinsic object for, not a property of the object or the state.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sort-extensible" step="2" class="history">Whether an object without an [[Extensible]] internal slot has been observed to return *false* from [[IsExtensible]] or *true* from [[PreventExtensions]]: the answers of earlier calls, which the state does not record.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="ph-twenty-significant-digits" step="2" class="assert-provenance">_n_ is a decimal literal's value at every use; an existential over all integers with no test over an abstract mathematical value.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-number.prototype.toexponential#1" step="1" class="informative">The NOTE's alternative to the step choosing _exponent_, _intSignificand_ and _ff_, recommended as a guideline only.</emu-permanent>
  <emu-permanent clause="sec-numeric-types-number-tostring#1" step="1" class="informative">The NOTE's alternative to the step choosing _n_, _k_ and _s_, recommended as a guideline only.</emu-permanent>
</emu-clause>
